<title>BELGIUM: Belgian federal spending rose in Jan-Nov 1996.</title>
<headline>Belgian federal spending rose in Jan-Nov 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Primary spending by the Belgian federal state rose to 964.0 billion francs in the first 11 months of 1996, compared with 944.4 billion in the year-earlier period, the budget ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>Corrected for inflation, this reflected a zero growth in budget spending, it said.</p>
<p>The statement said the increase in primary spending was entirely in line with the government's policy of holding growth in spending to at most the rate of inflation.</p>
